OL,3,GNEWSA'The school has gone': The cries
OL,4,Aheard by man who called 999 as Aberfan
OL,5,Adisaster unfolded
OL,6,
OL,7,F"There was a lady running up and down
OL,8,Fthe pavement here shouting, 'the school
OL,9,Fhas gone, the school has gone'."
OL,11,FNearly 60 years to the day, Dave Evans
OL,12,Fcan still hear the cries.
OL,14,FSitting outside his home in Aberfan, he
OL,15,Fpoints towards the street where panic
OL,16,Funfolded on the morning of 21 October
OL,17,F1966, when a collapsing coal waste tip
OL,18,Fengulfed Pantglas Junior School and
OL,19,Fnearby homes.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
